+
+R3's Immersive was a MODE on top of the selector holsters: grip = draw the
+zone's weapon, release = stow to the axe. the user's verdict was that this is not
+what holding a weapon means. v2 makes the holsters PHYSICAL:
+
+  * Two holsters, left hip and right hip. Each CONTAINS a weapon, or nothing.
+    (The shoulder and chest zones keep their geometry — Convenience still uses
+    all five — but they are dormant in this mode.)
+  * A holstered weapon is RENDERED: a floating model in its zone, vertical,
+    muzzle down. You can see what you are carrying by looking down.
+  * The grip only means anything INSIDE a zone. Empty hand in an occupied zone
+    takes; a held weapon in an empty zone stows; a held weapon in an occupied
+    zone SWAPS. The weapon stays in the hand afterwards without holding grip.
+  * EITHER hand. DUAL WIELD, different weapons only. Each trigger selects and
+    fires ITS OWN weapon; empty hands render nothing and their trigger is
+    suppressed, because firing an invisible weapon is the worst outcome here.
+  * The axe is an ordinary weapon: holsterable, holdable, never a fallback.
+
